nodecode-kiro-acp is a rewrite of tobenwarrior's tobenwarrior/hermes-kiro-provider:

https://github.com/tobenwarrior/hermes-kiro-provider
commit 02c4dd06585436751145961658a22b773f23a0ef
MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 tobenwarrior (LICENSE)

Rewritten: the provider a turn rides (a `kiro-cli acp' subprocess on the
user's own Kiro login), the ACP session lifecycle (initialize at protocol
version 1, session/new, the model and the reasoning effort as session config
options, one session/prompt per round), the fold of the streamed
session/update text into the turn, the OpenAI-schema prompt with the
<tool_call> block contract and its parsing back into tool calls, the
fs/read_text_file and fs/write_text_file bridge, the permission answer, the
rule that a turn naming the provider itself means the session's own model,
the argument list the section names, and the note when the CLI is missing
or logged out. Reimplemented in Common Lisp against the Nodecode cell
contract: one lane whose stream function spawns the CLI and speaks the
protocol, one hook answering the credential, one listing the models.

Left out: the plugin's inheritance of its harness's in-tree ACP client
(agent.copilot_acp_client) and the provider-profile plumbing that came with
it (the `kiro', `kiro-cli' and `kiro-acp-agent' aliases, the acp://kiro
marker base URL, the chat_completions api_mode); the live model catalog
fetched from a throwaway session/new and cached for an hour, which only fed
the harness's model picker (the section's `models' names the same thing
without spawning a process at listing time); the HERMES_KIRO_ACP_COMMAND,
KIRO_CLI_PATH and HERMES_KIRO_ACP_ARGS environment overrides, which the
section's `command' and `args' state; and the Copilot-flavored error
translation, replaced by the same note at the point of failure.
